      en: "Exchange Square in Central, Hong Kong, is a business complex comprising two office towers and a public plaza. Completed in 1985, Tower One is 188 meters and Tower Two 169 meters tall. The complex houses the Hong Kong Stock Exchange (HKEX), one of the world's largest stock exchanges by market capitalization. The plaza features artwork and a fountain. Exchange Square is a hub for financial activity, with a daily trading volume in the billions. It connects directly to the MTR and the International Finance Centre. The complex symbolizes Hong Kong's status as a global financial center.",
